WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.914
A compound works at nanomolar concentration in a

00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:07.269
protected assay. The number is seductive, but a

00:00:07.269 --> 00:00:07.769
patient

00:00:07.769 --> 00:00:09.872
never receives an assay plate.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.538
Solubility, absorption, distribution, metabolism and

00:00:19.538 --> 00:00:22.612
clearance decide whether the required free

00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:23.564
concentration

00:00:23.564 --> 00:00:24.930
reaches the tissue.

00:00:30.758 --> 00:00:34.204
A high tissue or plasma concentration can conceal

00:00:34.204 --> 00:00:38.070
extensive binding. Free exposure at the site of action

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:38.213
is

00:00:38.213 --> 00:00:39.760
the relevant question.

00:00:45.508 --> 00:00:48.895
Ask what dose achieves occupancy for long enough, and

00:00:48.895 --> 00:00:51.951
what happens elsewhere in the body at that same

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:52.536
exposure.

00:00:57.217 --> 00:01:00.337
Potency cannot compensate indefinitely for

00:01:00.337 --> 00:01:01.228
permeability

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:04.875
barriers, toxicity or infeasible pharmacokinetics.

00:01:09.883 --> 00:01:13.239
The argument is about choosing compounds that can

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:13.718
deliver

00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:17.351
an effective unbound concentration, not applauding the

00:01:17.351 --> 00:01:18.831
smallest assay number.
